# Rust / Tauri build output
src-tauri/target/

# Tauri-generated ACL/permission schemas (regenerated by `tauri-build` on every build)
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
# Same generated-by-tauri-build category, current tauri-build (2.6.3) writes it here too.
src-tauri/permissions/autogenerated/

# Local bundles
src-tauri/bundle/

# Staged runtime (podman + machine image) — fetched + sha256-verified by
# scripts/stage-runtime.sh from the committed runtime-manifest.lock. Never
# committed: it is large (tens to hundreds of MB per target) and fully
# reproducible from the lock file. Contains ONLY extracted/normalized files —
# see .cache/ below for why raw download archives must NEVER live here too.
src-tauri/resources/runtime/

# Raw download cache (.tgz/.zip/.pkg/.part) for scripts/stage-runtime.sh —
# deliberately OUTSIDE src-tauri/resources/runtime/: that whole tree gets
# glob-matched into the .app bundle (tauri.bundle.conf.json), and a real
# macOS notarization run rejected the app because an archive nested there
# (even gitignored) was swept in and its unsigned contents inspected. Never
# move this back under src-tauri/resources/ — see stage-runtime.sh's own
# comment on CACHE_DIR and tests/test-packaged-layout.sh.
.cache/
